1
00:00:00,617 --> 00:00:03,826
(One Step Closer)

2
00:00:03,827 --> 00:00:05,126
Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:05,127 --> 00:00:07,326
(Nice to see you all.)

4
00:00:07,327 --> 00:00:08,826
It's been a while, Joy.

5
00:00:08,827 --> 00:00:11,067
- Yes, it's been so long. - It's been a while.

6
00:00:11,197 --> 00:00:14,067
I watched the preview of the show last week.

7
00:00:14,397 --> 00:00:16,537
- You went to meet Ito Junji. - Right.

8
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,136
(Exploding with anticipation)

9
00:00:19,137 --> 00:00:20,137
- You went on a trip. - He's the master artist.

10
00:00:20,138 --> 00:00:22,546
Actually, people around my age...

11
00:00:22,547 --> 00:00:25,047
love Ito Junji and his works.

12
00:00:25,447 --> 00:00:26,947
We grew up reading "Uzumaki," "Tomie,"

13
00:00:27,347 --> 00:00:28,817
and other series of his.

14
00:00:29,687 --> 00:00:30,816
I wanted to style myself like Tomie back in the day.

15
00:00:30,817 --> 00:00:32,886
- She had such fair skin. - Right, there's a resemblance.

16
00:00:32,887 --> 00:00:34,057
- Really? - There's a resemblance.

17
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:35,486
Whenever I get bangs,

18
00:00:35,487 --> 00:00:38,327
I want to style myself like her no matter what.

19
00:00:38,427 --> 00:00:39,897
You know what?

20
00:00:40,397 --> 00:00:41,797
- I can't picture it. - Okay.

21
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:42,896
- I've never seen him. - Right.

22
00:00:42,897 --> 00:00:44,266
- The artist? - Yes, the artist.

23
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:45,597
The fact that...

24
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:48,137
- he agreed to see me... - Right. Picturing that...

25
00:00:48,837 --> 00:00:50,967
- I don't know what to say. - It doesn't feel real.

26
00:00:51,137 --> 00:00:54,607
Picture a major national holiday like Lunar New Year.

27
00:00:55,707 --> 00:00:58,077
So you're doing the New Year's bow, and there's Beckham sitting there.

28
00:00:58,847 --> 00:01:00,346
- It's... - It feels that unrealistic?

29
00:01:00,347 --> 00:01:01,416
It does.

30
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:03,187
That's how it feels to me.

31
00:01:04,887 --> 00:01:06,416
(Longtime Admiration)

32
00:01:06,417 --> 00:01:07,517
"Longtime Admiration."

33
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:18,767
(Kian84 walks through the big crowd.)

34
00:01:19,797 --> 00:01:21,637
(Reading tensely)

35
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:24,706
"Where am I?"

36
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:26,107
"Where am I?"

37
00:01:27,377 --> 00:01:28,807
I'm in Japan.

38
00:01:29,277 --> 00:01:31,147
I came to Tokyo.

39
00:01:31,347 --> 00:01:32,747
Personally, I have huge respect for him.

40
00:01:33,377 --> 00:01:36,387
His name is Ito Junji.

41
00:01:36,617 --> 00:01:38,816
Kangnam said he would help me meet the artist,

42
00:01:38,817 --> 00:01:40,857
and set up a meeting.

43
00:01:41,357 --> 00:01:45,827
Then he really managed to get me a meeting with him.

44
00:01:46,127 --> 00:01:48,197
- He said he'd get me a meeting. - That's amazing.

45
00:01:48,397 --> 00:01:50,066
(He came to meet the man he's admired for a long time.)

46
00:01:50,067 --> 00:01:51,127
So I'm here.

47
00:01:51,997 --> 00:01:53,997
(The artist made a debut in 1987 with "Tomie.")

48
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:57,007
(His unique styles and plots...)

49
00:01:58,167 --> 00:01:59,277
That's from "Uzumaki."

50
00:02:00,137 --> 00:02:01,476
("Ito Junji Wins the Eisner Award for Best Edition")

51
00:02:01,477 --> 00:02:02,746
("Ito Junji, the Master of Horror, Wins 2 Eisner Awards")

52
00:02:02,747 --> 00:02:04,107
("Ito Junji's Work Gains Worldwide Recognition")

53
00:02:04,777 --> 00:02:05,946
("He was inducted into the Will Eisner Awards Hall of Fame")

54
00:02:05,947 --> 00:02:07,077
(It's equivalent to the Academy Awards.)

55
00:02:08,117 --> 00:02:10,817
(The master artist of horror manga, Ito Junji)

56
00:02:11,417 --> 00:02:14,257
As a little kid, I used to read a lot of comic books.

57
00:02:14,457 --> 00:02:15,526
There were many series...

58
00:02:15,527 --> 00:02:17,387
such as "Dragon Ball," Slam Dunk," and "One Piece."

59
00:02:17,727 --> 00:02:18,757
Personally,

60
00:02:18,897 --> 00:02:22,567
I loved Ito Junji's manga series...

61
00:02:22,697 --> 00:02:24,667
because his story development was so original.

62
00:02:24,937 --> 00:02:26,437
The basic format of comics went like this.

63
00:02:26,767 --> 00:02:28,066
Once the main character beat an opponent,

64
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:29,366
a strong opponent showed up next.

65
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:31,407
The story focused on highlighting the growth of the character.

66
00:02:31,977 --> 00:02:34,437
But in Ito Junji's series,

67
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,276
the plots were developed...

68
00:02:36,277 --> 00:02:37,847
and were interpreted in a completely different way.

69
00:02:38,207 --> 00:02:40,046
So I can't simply call them horror mango.

70
00:02:40,047 --> 00:02:41,817
- Right. - I wouldn't even call it horror.

71
00:02:42,347 --> 00:02:44,386
I had never seen anything like that before.

72
00:02:44,387 --> 00:02:45,616
- He created his own genre. - I agree.

73
00:02:45,617 --> 00:02:47,587
Ito Junji is his own genre.

74
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:48,986
- Right. - Yes.

75
00:02:48,987 --> 00:02:49,987
No one can compare.

76
00:02:49,988 --> 00:02:51,727
His manga series influenced me as an artist too.

77
00:02:52,857 --> 00:02:54,997
As a kid, I enjoyed reading his manga series.

78
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:57,397
Even after I became a webtoon artist,

79
00:02:57,597 --> 00:02:59,297
I kept following his career.

80
00:02:59,867 --> 00:03:01,037
I like Ito Junji.

81
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:03,207
(He expressed his admiration of the artist to Kangnam.)

82
00:03:03,937 --> 00:03:08,107
(I'll help you meet him.)

83
00:03:08,307 --> 00:03:09,577
I just have to finish this.

84
00:03:10,477 --> 00:03:11,546
- He made a call right away? - What?

85
00:03:11,547 --> 00:03:13,117
(Are you making a call?)

86
00:03:13,677 --> 00:03:14,946
(Is this Ito Junji's agency?)

87
00:03:14,947 --> 00:03:16,047
- Kangnam... - What?

88
00:03:16,387 --> 00:03:17,947
(Nervous)

89
00:03:18,457 --> 00:03:21,617
(Do you mean Ito Junji, not Inagawa Junji?)

90
00:03:22,327 --> 00:03:26,357
(Who's this guy? I don't know who he is.)

91
00:03:27,097 --> 00:03:29,166
(Manga artist: Ito Junji, Horror storyteller: Inagawa Junji)

92
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,566
When you turn on the TV at night during summertime in Japan,

93
00:03:31,567 --> 00:03:32,697
he's always on TV.

94
00:03:32,997 --> 00:03:34,397
I guess he's a famous guy.

95
00:03:35,737 --> 00:03:37,566
(Let's get you a meeting with the manga artist.)

96
00:03:37,567 --> 00:03:39,137
(I'll talk to him for you.)

97
00:03:39,407 --> 00:03:41,977
When he said he'd help me meet him,

98
00:03:43,277 --> 00:03:45,347
- I was skeptical. - You didn't make much of it.

99
00:03:45,577 --> 00:03:47,177
I'm a huge fan.

100
00:03:47,617 --> 00:03:49,047
So I try to follow him online.

101
00:03:49,447 --> 00:03:51,686
- But he rarely posts things online. - Right.

102
00:03:51,687 --> 00:03:52,717
That's why...

103
00:03:53,257 --> 00:03:55,286
if I'm being honest,

104
00:03:55,287 --> 00:03:57,286
I never imagined I would be able to meet him.

105
00:03:57,287 --> 00:03:59,827
Well, we move in completely different circles.

106
00:04:00,127 --> 00:04:02,267
I never thought I would be able to meet him.

107
00:04:03,497 --> 00:04:05,537
I was still skeptical even during the interview.

108
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:07,597
- Even after arriving in Japan? - Yes.

109
00:04:07,797 --> 00:04:09,736
- Kangnam loves pranking people. - Right.

110
00:04:09,737 --> 00:04:11,366
He might introduce his friend named Junji.

111
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:13,006
("This is my friend, Junji, not Ito Junji.")

112
00:04:13,007 --> 00:04:14,037
Seriously.

113
00:04:14,237 --> 00:04:16,077
- I would've gotten physical then. - "This is my friend, Ito Junji."

114
00:04:16,207 --> 00:04:17,846
- Right. That must be a common name. - Of course.

115
00:04:17,847 --> 00:04:18,877
It's a common name.

116
00:04:20,777 --> 00:04:21,946
(He flew to Japan to meet the manga artist.)

117
00:04:21,947 --> 00:04:24,017
- You went there only with a bag? - Yes.

118
00:04:26,517 --> 00:04:28,157
"Hamamatsucho Station."

119
00:04:29,987 --> 00:04:31,556
I guess you're taking the subway.

120
00:04:31,557 --> 00:04:33,357
Yes. Taxis in Japan are expensive.

121
00:04:35,297 --> 00:04:37,597
Insert cash or a credit card.

122
00:04:38,597 --> 00:04:39,966
(He follows the voice guidance to buy the ticket.)

123
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:41,867
The ticket machines offer Korean translation these days.

124
00:04:41,967 --> 00:04:42,967
Right.

125
00:04:43,807 --> 00:04:45,907
Will this get me to my destination?

126
00:04:46,177 --> 00:04:47,907
- My gosh. - What?

127
00:04:48,277 --> 00:04:49,707
What? Oh, are you Korean?

128
00:04:50,347 --> 00:04:51,676
- Ma'am. - Yes.

129
00:04:51,677 --> 00:04:53,576
- What? - There's this monorail.

130
00:04:53,577 --> 00:04:56,017
- Can I get on it with this? - There's a Korean worker.

131
00:04:56,747 --> 00:04:59,017
You can take the next one. It's express, so it's quicker.

132
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:00,386
- I see. - Scan it.

133
00:05:00,387 --> 00:05:02,026
- Scan it when you get off too. - Okay.

134
00:05:02,027 --> 00:05:03,356
- Thank you. - Happy New Year.

135
00:05:03,357 --> 00:05:04,487
- Happy New Year. - Thanks.

136
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:11,167
I wanted to use some Japanese phrases I learned.

137
00:05:12,497 --> 00:05:13,837
It's like I'm at Seoul Station.

138
00:05:16,307 --> 00:05:18,067
There are many subway trains.

139
00:05:20,807 --> 00:05:24,207
(He gets on the train while mumbling Japanese to himself.)

140
00:05:30,317 --> 00:05:33,057
You must start to feel nervous on the train.

141
00:05:35,257 --> 00:05:37,627
(Heading downtown with excitement and nervousness)

142
00:05:39,527 --> 00:05:41,996
- I just noticed your sweatshirt... - Right.

143
00:05:41,997 --> 00:05:44,096
- is Ito Junji's merchandise. Right? - Right.

144
00:05:44,097 --> 00:05:45,567
("Souichi's Diary of Curses")

145
00:05:47,337 --> 00:05:48,937
My gosh, cherry blossoms are already in bloom.

146
00:05:50,167 --> 00:05:51,206
Already?

147
00:05:51,207 --> 00:05:52,777
(The flowers are in full bloom like his heart.)

148
00:05:53,507 --> 00:05:54,907
The flowers have bloomed.

149
00:05:57,447 --> 00:05:58,646
The flowers have bloomed.

150
00:05:58,647 --> 00:06:00,817
(Japan and my heart are in spring.)

151
00:06:02,687 --> 00:06:03,947
It feels like I'm dreaming.

152
00:06:04,817 --> 00:06:05,987
It's so romantic right now.

153
00:06:06,387 --> 00:06:07,457
It's like a scene from a Japanese movie.

154
00:06:11,527 --> 00:06:14,556
(Ito Junji...)

155
00:06:14,557 --> 00:06:17,897
(and Kian84)

156
00:06:19,397 --> 00:06:21,796
(Now...)

157
00:06:21,797 --> 00:06:23,507
He's on his way now.

158
00:06:26,777 --> 00:06:28,776
I look pretty cool in this clip.

159
00:06:28,777 --> 00:06:30,047
What a surprise choice of music for Kian84.

160
00:06:30,747 --> 00:06:32,247
Personally, I have huge respect for him.

161
00:06:32,377 --> 00:06:34,417
He's a manga artist.

162
00:06:34,777 --> 00:06:36,217
It feels like I'm dreaming right now.

163
00:06:36,817 --> 00:06:39,157
I bet. It must feel so surreal.

164
00:06:43,587 --> 00:06:44,627
Is this the place?

165
00:06:45,057 --> 00:06:46,497
"Log."

166
00:06:47,797 --> 00:06:50,696
(He goes straight to a building without any hesitation.)

167
00:06:50,697 --> 00:06:51,767
- What? - What?

168
00:06:52,897 --> 00:06:53,997
This is the place.

169
00:06:54,237 --> 00:06:57,707
- You're meeting him there? - No, I won't go to his house.

170
00:06:58,367 --> 00:07:00,477
He wouldn't just barge into someone's home.

171
00:07:00,707 --> 00:07:02,006
And bang on his door?

172
00:07:02,007 --> 00:07:03,147
"Junji!"

173
00:07:03,577 --> 00:07:04,647
"Junji."

174
00:07:05,317 --> 00:07:06,476
(What?)

175
00:07:06,477 --> 00:07:07,547
That would be random.

176
00:07:07,647 --> 00:07:09,087
That's my lodging.

177
00:07:09,517 --> 00:07:11,346
- I need to get ready first. - Of course.

178
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,557
I'm meeting him the next day. This is only my first day.

179
00:07:13,857 --> 00:07:16,087
I can't pound on his door as soon as I get there.

180
00:07:16,457 --> 00:07:18,257
- I can picture you doing that. - Gosh, no.

181
00:07:18,757 --> 00:07:19,957
I'm more socially adapted now.

182
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,166
This is the place.

183
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:25,667
(He checks in first like a well-mannered man.)

184
00:07:26,967 --> 00:07:28,866
I see. This is the place.

185
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:29,906
(He booked a house in advance.)

186
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:30,937
This is nice.

187
00:07:33,237 --> 00:07:35,277
- He found a cute and cozy place. - Yes.

188
00:07:38,917 --> 00:07:40,116
I see tatami too.

189
00:07:40,117 --> 00:07:41,517
(The 2nd-floor bedroom is covered with tatami.)

190
00:07:42,217 --> 00:07:45,216
Hotels look the same. You know?

191
00:07:45,217 --> 00:07:47,457
Even the layout and service are similar.

192
00:07:47,757 --> 00:07:50,587
I wanted to get the local vibe, so I rented a house instead.

193
00:07:50,957 --> 00:07:52,396
The units on the platform were spacious and cheap.

194
00:07:52,397 --> 00:07:53,526
- It's a great platform. - Right.

195
00:07:53,527 --> 00:07:54,597
They're better than hotels.

196
00:07:56,697 --> 00:07:58,766
What's this? It's the bathroom.

197
00:07:58,767 --> 00:08:00,637
(He checks the bathroom first.)

198
00:08:01,097 --> 00:08:02,637
Gosh, look at all these stairs.

199
00:08:03,937 --> 00:08:06,707
- That's a typical house in Japan. - Stairs...

200
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,837
I see.

201
00:08:12,247 --> 00:08:15,987
(Drawing open the curtains first)

202
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:20,816
(Let me open up the windows too.)

203
00:08:20,817 --> 00:08:22,557
It looks like a house you'd see in Japanese movies.

204
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:25,527
(Sitting down)

205
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:31,497
(He organizes his belongings as soon as he sits down.)

206
00:08:33,437 --> 00:08:34,967
It's wrinkled. Darn it.

207
00:08:35,067 --> 00:08:36,337
- Oh, my. - You packed a button-down shirt.

208
00:08:38,907 --> 00:08:40,677
You had a button-down shirt in the bag? Oh, my.

209
00:08:41,537 --> 00:08:44,107
What's that? Things keep on coming out of that bag.

210
00:08:44,207 --> 00:08:45,947
- Where did he get the jacket? - I was so surprised.

211
00:08:48,377 --> 00:08:49,947
How did you pull out a suit from that bag?

212
00:08:50,217 --> 00:08:51,987
You can stay in my bag if you want.

213
00:08:52,457 --> 00:08:53,517
Everything can fit in the bag.

214
00:08:54,917 --> 00:08:56,256
Hey, it's not wrinkled at all.

215
00:08:56,257 --> 00:08:57,327
(He carefully brought a suit and a tie.)

216
00:08:58,027 --> 00:09:01,557
I only wear suits once a year for the year-end awards ceremony.

217
00:09:02,097 --> 00:09:04,527
I don't even wear a suit to weddings.

218
00:09:05,027 --> 00:09:06,197
I rarely wear suits.

219
00:09:08,037 --> 00:09:09,136
That was a long time ago.

220
00:09:09,137 --> 00:09:10,367
What's wrong with my face?

221
00:09:11,907 --> 00:09:14,577
(Gosh, come on.)

222
00:09:14,737 --> 00:09:15,807
Did I get stung by a bee?

223
00:09:16,247 --> 00:09:17,377
You looked so chubby then.

224
00:09:18,077 --> 00:09:19,347
That was ten years ago.

225
00:09:19,677 --> 00:09:20,947
- Ten years ago? - Yes.

226
00:09:21,547 --> 00:09:24,686
I'm finally meeting the artist I've wanted to meet most.

227
00:09:24,687 --> 00:09:26,716
I didn't think it was polite of me...

228
00:09:26,717 --> 00:09:28,387
to show up in a casual outfit.

229
00:09:28,657 --> 00:09:30,856
I wanted to look neat for him.

230
00:09:30,857 --> 00:09:31,886
Right.

231
00:09:31,887 --> 00:09:33,597
(I brought a suit to look neat.)

232
00:09:35,097 --> 00:09:38,367
(He finishes putting away his things after hanging up the suit.)

233
00:09:43,767 --> 00:09:46,907
(Staring out the window)

234
00:09:48,107 --> 00:09:53,077
(I can't believe I'm here in Japan to meet him.)

235
00:09:56,787 --> 00:09:58,816
(He feels the relaxed vibe of Tokyo through the window.)

236
00:09:58,817 --> 00:10:00,016
- What a nice atmosphere. - Right.

237
00:10:00,017 --> 00:10:01,687
(He feels the relaxed vibe of Tokyo through the window.)

238
00:10:03,427 --> 00:10:05,657
(Slurping)

239
00:10:06,197 --> 00:10:08,897
(He fills his stomach with cup noodles.)

240
00:10:09,827 --> 00:10:11,367
(Slurping)

241
00:10:13,937 --> 00:10:15,737
(Munching)

242
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:19,707
(Drinking up the broth too)

243
00:10:20,277 --> 00:10:21,337
I'm stuffed.

244
00:10:23,577 --> 00:10:26,777
(He grabs a quick meal with cup noodles.)

245
00:10:28,647 --> 00:10:31,747
(He grabs a box and climbs the stairs.)

246
00:10:32,157 --> 00:10:33,287
Gosh, it's cold.

247
00:10:37,927 --> 00:10:41,257
(Plopping down)

248
00:10:43,267 --> 00:10:45,937
(Staring)

249
00:10:47,067 --> 00:10:48,297
Questions for him...

250
00:10:51,507 --> 00:10:53,107
(Hello. It's nice to meet you.)

251
00:10:53,977 --> 00:10:55,036
I studied a bit.

252
00:10:55,037 --> 00:10:57,077
(A long list of questions)

253
00:10:58,247 --> 00:11:00,877
"It feels like a dream to meet you."

254
00:11:01,717 --> 00:11:02,786
"It feels like..."

255
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:05,417
(It feels like a dream.)

256
00:11:06,117 --> 00:11:07,887
"It feels like a dream."

257
00:11:09,557 --> 00:11:11,787
I grew up reading your comics.

258
00:11:12,197 --> 00:11:15,797
So I became a manga artist.

259
00:11:16,627 --> 00:11:19,167
Later on, you had a huge influence on me.

260
00:11:20,097 --> 00:11:21,196
I was informed...

261
00:11:21,197 --> 00:11:23,067
about three months ago that I'd be able to meet him.

262
00:11:23,667 --> 00:11:25,807
I've been studying Japanese quite diligently...

263
00:11:26,237 --> 00:11:27,707
after hearing the news.

264
00:11:27,877 --> 00:11:30,976
I spent as much time studying Japanese as running...

265
00:11:30,977 --> 00:11:31,977
- because... - You studied that much?

266
00:11:31,978 --> 00:11:35,147
he put aside time for our meeting.

267
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,516
I didn't want to look silly...

268
00:11:36,517 --> 00:11:38,587
and make mistakes while speaking in Japanese.

269
00:11:39,587 --> 00:11:41,656
I wrote down a lot of things I wanted to tell him.

270
00:11:41,657 --> 00:11:43,357
I practiced a lot too.

271
00:11:45,027 --> 00:11:47,127
If I studied this hard when I was young...

272
00:11:48,257 --> 00:11:49,727
Well, I still wouldn't have been able to get into SNU.

273
00:11:49,797 --> 00:11:51,427
Anyway, the point is...

274
00:11:52,367 --> 00:11:55,097
I studied a lot and became to enjoy it.

275
00:11:55,197 --> 00:11:56,337
So I kept studying it.

276
00:11:57,207 --> 00:12:01,707
"I think it was around 1994."

277
00:12:02,077 --> 00:12:04,307
"I saw your manga series in an old bookstore..."

278
00:12:05,207 --> 00:12:06,377
"For the first time."

279
00:12:07,817 --> 00:12:08,887
"For the first time."

280
00:12:10,447 --> 00:12:16,427
(He looks up the words he doesn't know.)

281
00:12:17,327 --> 00:12:20,356
(Unlike 6 months ago...)

282
00:12:20,357 --> 00:12:24,567
(when he could only list simple words in Japanese,)

283
00:12:25,127 --> 00:12:26,437
"I saw it for the first time."

284
00:12:27,937 --> 00:12:30,706
(it's quite an improvement.)

285
00:12:30,707 --> 00:12:32,376
He's serious about learning Japanese.

286
00:12:32,377 --> 00:12:33,606
He was studying in his waiting room too.

287
00:12:33,607 --> 00:12:34,636
(Impressed)

288
00:12:34,637 --> 00:12:35,707
It all started with you.

289
00:12:36,807 --> 00:12:39,047
I always saw you studying in your spare time.

290
00:12:41,077 --> 00:12:43,116
"How are things with you these days?"

291
00:12:43,117 --> 00:12:44,247
(He keeps practicing the questions.)

292
00:12:44,817 --> 00:12:47,687
"Out of all your manga characters,"

293
00:12:47,917 --> 00:12:50,057
"my favorite one is Souichi."

294
00:12:50,927 --> 00:12:53,857
This character right here is my favorite character.

295
00:12:55,727 --> 00:12:56,897
His name is Souichi.

296
00:12:57,167 --> 00:13:00,096
He's always low on iron, so he always has nails in his mouth.

297
00:13:00,097 --> 00:13:01,197
He's low on iron?

298
00:13:01,437 --> 00:13:03,067
He's quite twisted too.

299
00:13:03,567 --> 00:13:06,037
He reminds me of myself when I was young.

300
00:13:06,507 --> 00:13:08,706
I'm getting the feeling that he might have been...

301
00:13:08,707 --> 00:13:10,907
like Souichi when he was young too.

302
00:13:12,777 --> 00:13:14,747
How old is he?

303
00:13:16,887 --> 00:13:19,456
He was born in 1963. So he's 21 years older than me.

304
00:13:19,457 --> 00:13:21,616
- He's the same age as my mother. - He's about the same age as my mom.

305
00:13:21,617 --> 00:13:23,526
- Really? - He's 64 years old?

306
00:13:23,527 --> 00:13:25,857
(He's 64 years old?)

307
00:13:25,997 --> 00:13:28,967
I should ask him about his health then.

308
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:32,436
"Your health." That's the word.

309
00:13:32,437 --> 00:13:34,167
(He adds more questions out of sincerity.)

310
00:13:35,567 --> 00:13:37,307
"How is your cat doing?"

311
00:13:38,007 --> 00:13:39,807
"What kind of student were you in school?"

312
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:41,937
"Do you still draw?"

313
00:13:43,207 --> 00:13:44,307
"Lastly,"

314
00:13:45,477 --> 00:13:49,587
"how do you want the world to remember you?"

315
00:13:51,387 --> 00:13:53,186
(Getting sentimental)

316
00:13:53,187 --> 00:13:56,786
That reminds me of something. My fans from abroad...

317
00:13:56,787 --> 00:13:58,556
always study Korean...

318
00:13:58,557 --> 00:13:59,796
- Right. - and practice the sentences,

319
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:00,997
so they can speak Korean to me.

320
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:02,867
- That's touching. - I can picture my fans...

321
00:14:03,067 --> 00:14:04,626
- Right. - studying like him.

322
00:14:04,627 --> 00:14:07,836
- This is such a touching moment. - Same here. This is so touching.

323
00:14:07,837 --> 00:14:10,666
Both of your fans from Japan practice Korean...

324
00:14:10,667 --> 00:14:11,966
- out of love for you guys. - Right.

325
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:13,477
- Right. They practice Korean. - They study Korean for you.

326
00:14:13,877 --> 00:14:15,607
- Right. - I never thought...

327
00:14:15,947 --> 00:14:17,346
- I'd be anyone's fan. But I was. - Exactly.

328
00:14:17,347 --> 00:14:19,077
- You're his fan. - Right. After all these years.

329
00:14:19,177 --> 00:14:21,376
It's rare to feel those emotions after getting old.

330
00:14:21,377 --> 00:14:23,187
Right. I don't think I had that experience.

331
00:14:24,247 --> 00:14:27,687
If I need more help, I'll try to be more flexible when I meet him.

332
00:14:30,692 --> 00:14:31,792
(Ripping open)

333
00:14:33,102 --> 00:14:34,201
(Why is he suddenly opening up a box?)

334
00:14:34,202 --> 00:14:35,262
What?

335
00:14:36,432 --> 00:14:38,672
(Reaching)

336
00:14:41,272 --> 00:14:42,442
You got a canvas.

337
00:14:42,912 --> 00:14:44,442
- You're going to paint there? - Yes.

338
00:14:44,642 --> 00:14:46,212
(He gently tosses the canvas on the floor.)

339
00:14:46,682 --> 00:14:50,282
(He fills the ramyeon cup with water and comes upstairs.)

340
00:14:51,552 --> 00:14:52,782
Oh, my.

341
00:14:56,222 --> 00:14:59,092
(He grabs the tablet PC.)

342
00:15:00,122 --> 00:15:02,222
(Let's see.)

343
00:15:02,692 --> 00:15:03,992
Ito Junji.

344
00:15:05,492 --> 00:15:07,061
(He looks up pictures of Ito Junji online.)

345
00:15:07,062 --> 00:15:08,802
I see. You'll paint him a portrait?

346
00:15:10,832 --> 00:15:13,642
I grew up reading...

347
00:15:14,242 --> 00:15:16,312
Ito Junji's manga series.

348
00:15:16,812 --> 00:15:18,812
That inspired me to draw later in my life.

349
00:15:19,682 --> 00:15:23,352
I thought giving him a painting as a gift would be a nice gesture.

350
00:15:24,152 --> 00:15:27,252
- He must feel so proud. - So I painted.

351
00:15:30,152 --> 00:15:31,221
Health.

352
00:15:31,222 --> 00:15:32,561
(What should I paint?)

353
00:15:32,562 --> 00:15:33,621
It's the Year of the Horse.

354
00:15:33,622 --> 00:15:35,092
(A painting for good health or the Year of the Horse?)

355
00:15:36,162 --> 00:15:37,361
It must've been so hard to decide.

356
00:15:37,362 --> 00:15:39,032
- It was going to be a present. - Right.

357
00:15:39,162 --> 00:15:40,902
I was planning to give it to a manga artist I admired.

358
00:15:41,202 --> 00:15:42,361
So I had a hard time deciding.

359
00:15:42,362 --> 00:15:45,272
And giving a painting to a well-respected artist isn't easy.

360
00:15:46,602 --> 00:15:49,572
(Let me start painting.)

361
00:15:50,412 --> 00:15:52,442
(He grabs the paint after thinking for a while.)

362
00:15:54,012 --> 00:15:56,882
(He puts a blob of paint on the canvas.)

363
00:15:59,652 --> 00:16:03,622
(He calmly starts painting.)

364
00:16:05,992 --> 00:16:10,492
(He highlights his unique painting style.)

365
00:16:13,232 --> 00:16:17,172
(Then he sighs.)

366
00:16:21,442 --> 00:16:24,872
(Just as he gets into it, he suddenly stops.)

367
00:16:25,342 --> 00:16:26,681
You have a lot on your mind, right?

368
00:16:26,682 --> 00:16:27,911
- Yes, I had a lot on my mind. - Right.

369
00:16:27,912 --> 00:16:29,312
It's tough when you have a lot on your mind.

370
00:16:29,912 --> 00:16:31,212
Painting for...

371
00:16:33,652 --> 00:16:35,922
a manga artist I admire is not easy.

372
00:16:47,032 --> 00:16:49,471
(He puts down the paintbrush...)

373
00:16:49,472 --> 00:16:51,732
(and grabs the paint tube again.)

374
00:17:00,442 --> 00:17:02,181
(He starts covering it up with the brush without hesitation.)

375
00:17:02,182 --> 00:17:03,411
- There's no hesitation. - Why are you doing that?

376
00:17:03,412 --> 00:17:04,751
- Covering up? - You just covered up...

377
00:17:04,752 --> 00:17:06,322
- the sketch with the paint? - Right.

378
00:17:06,422 --> 00:17:07,552
He didn't like it.

379
00:17:08,722 --> 00:17:10,651
(He covers it up completely.)

380
00:17:10,652 --> 00:17:12,092
It was...

381
00:17:12,152 --> 00:17:14,621
I mean, other fans must've given him their artworks as presents.

382
00:17:14,622 --> 00:17:16,862
I didn't want mine to look similar to theirs.

383
00:17:17,292 --> 00:17:20,932
I worked especially hard on the painting.

384
00:17:22,132 --> 00:17:24,171
(The painting goes back to square one just like that.)

385
00:17:24,172 --> 00:17:26,742
(Great. Let me start over.)

386
00:17:28,002 --> 00:17:30,012
(Ripping)

387
00:17:31,242 --> 00:17:34,912
(He squeezes paint onto the torn cardboard.)

388
00:17:36,352 --> 00:17:38,582
(Focused)

389
00:17:40,422 --> 00:17:42,251
(He starts painting after thinking for a while.)

390
00:17:42,252 --> 00:17:43,752
I wonder what he's going to paint.

391
00:17:45,322 --> 00:17:47,692
(Smiling)

392
00:17:48,592 --> 00:17:52,761
I've given away a lot of my paintings as presents.

393
00:17:52,762 --> 00:17:55,032
But the painting I did for him...

394
00:17:55,932 --> 00:17:57,401
was the most meaningful one.

395
00:17:57,402 --> 00:17:59,472
I worked really hard on the painting.

396
00:18:00,072 --> 00:18:03,311
He showed me how amazing manga artists could be...

397
00:18:03,312 --> 00:18:05,912
and how cool it was to have this career.

398
00:18:06,212 --> 00:18:08,542
He inspired me to see that.

399
00:18:12,822 --> 00:18:16,292
(Kian84 slowly gets into it.)

400
00:18:17,092 --> 00:18:19,592
Do I have hand tremors? Why are they shaking so much?

401
00:18:21,092 --> 00:18:22,461
(He saw countless pictures of his idol.)

402
00:18:22,462 --> 00:18:23,592
Gosh, I'm...

403
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,232
Oh, my back.

404
00:18:29,832 --> 00:18:31,971
(He endures the back pain due to the uncomfortable posture...)

405
00:18:31,972 --> 00:18:33,102
(and focuses on the painting again.)

406
00:18:34,442 --> 00:18:38,572
(Like Tokyo's deep-blue night,)

407
00:18:40,382 --> 00:18:43,982
(his painting gradually darkens.)

408
00:18:48,582 --> 00:18:51,252
(He doesn't lose focusing until the end and forgets the back pain.)

409
00:18:57,692 --> 00:19:02,902
(He signs his name in the corner of the canvas.)

410
00:19:12,742 --> 00:19:15,142
- I got goosebumps. - He's going to love it.

411
00:19:15,242 --> 00:19:18,382
Ito Junji reminds me of space.

412
00:19:18,952 --> 00:19:22,021
So I went with the shades of blue to represent space.

413
00:19:22,022 --> 00:19:23,892
I added swirling patterns on the side.

414
00:19:24,592 --> 00:19:26,562
He draws people in.

415
00:19:27,592 --> 00:19:29,562
His work...

416
00:19:30,132 --> 00:19:32,902
kind of reminds me of space.

417
00:19:33,302 --> 00:19:35,132
He pulls people in like a black hole.

418
00:19:35,932 --> 00:19:36,972
That's who he is to me.

419
00:19:37,272 --> 00:19:39,601
You compared him to space. That's just...

420
00:19:39,602 --> 00:19:40,672
I'm done.

421
00:19:41,102 --> 00:19:42,342
Oh, my back.

422
00:19:43,172 --> 00:19:44,242
My goodness, my back.

423
00:19:46,242 --> 00:19:48,411
(He finally stretches his back after finishing the painting.)

424
00:19:48,412 --> 00:19:49,552
I'm so tired.

425
00:19:51,112 --> 00:19:52,481
Oh, my. My back hurts.

426
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:55,122
(In no time, the night deepens like space.)

427
00:19:56,222 --> 00:19:58,422
(Impressed)

428
00:19:59,592 --> 00:20:00,861
- I just got goosebumps. - You did an amazing job.

429
00:20:00,862 --> 00:20:02,491
- Right. - I thought it was a picture.

430
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:03,531
Right.

431
00:20:03,532 --> 00:20:04,831
We all know how talented you are.

432
00:20:04,832 --> 00:20:06,261
But because you put your heart into it,

433
00:20:06,262 --> 00:20:07,432
it looks exceptional.

434
00:20:07,702 --> 00:20:10,472
I painted a younger version of him.

435
00:20:10,702 --> 00:20:12,502
- Look at the swirling patterns. - Gosh.

436
00:20:12,942 --> 00:20:14,301
How many hours did it take?

437
00:20:14,302 --> 00:20:16,372
About two and a half hours.

438
00:20:16,772 --> 00:20:17,872
That took a lot of time.

439
00:20:17,942 --> 00:20:20,481
When you did my portrait, you finished in an instant, right?

440
00:20:20,482 --> 00:20:21,582
I didn't try so hard on that one.

441
00:20:23,782 --> 00:20:25,282
He made me look like the root of a radish.

442
00:20:25,812 --> 00:20:28,452
My yard still scares me from time to time.

443
00:20:29,182 --> 00:20:31,592
(His half-hearted paintings are mentioned one after another.)

444
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:33,992
(The next day after a long day of painting)

445
00:20:34,992 --> 00:20:38,092
(He's going to meet Ito Junji today!)

446
00:20:39,962 --> 00:20:41,002
Gosh, it's cold.

447
00:20:43,172 --> 00:20:45,371
- It was so cold in Japan. - Right, it's cold there.

448
00:20:45,372 --> 00:20:47,142
You need to have layers of blankets too.

449
00:20:51,112 --> 00:20:53,042
I guess you didn't pack pajamas in your bag.

450
00:20:53,242 --> 00:20:55,112
(Embarrassed)

451
00:20:56,352 --> 00:20:58,682
(He wakes up while trembling in cold without pajamas.)

452
00:20:59,312 --> 00:21:00,722
(Sniffling)

453
00:21:01,022 --> 00:21:02,022
It's 9am.

454
00:21:04,022 --> 00:21:05,552
Gosh, I should get ready.

455
00:21:08,692 --> 00:21:11,031
- What? They're the same pants. - You're wearing dress pants?

456
00:21:11,032 --> 00:21:12,062
They're dress pants.

457
00:21:12,462 --> 00:21:14,031
(What is that?)

458
00:21:14,032 --> 00:21:16,731
- What? - I only brought one bag.

459
00:21:16,732 --> 00:21:18,472
I would have brought a suitcase if I packed extra pants.

460
00:21:18,932 --> 00:21:21,702
You must have ironed them before packing, right?

461
00:21:21,802 --> 00:21:23,211
- I didn't. - You didn't?

462
00:21:23,212 --> 00:21:25,471
I washed them after wearing them for a full week.

463
00:21:25,472 --> 00:21:27,181
- Well, pants... - So you just assume wearing them...

464
00:21:27,182 --> 00:21:29,211
- will get rid of the wrinkles? - Yes, that gets rid of wrinkles.

465
00:21:29,212 --> 00:21:30,752
Right. Spray some water, and the wrinkles are gone.

466
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:33,581
(He's wearing the dress pants he ironed last night.)

467
00:21:33,582 --> 00:21:35,782
- He wore them to sleep. - That's crazy.

468
00:21:36,052 --> 00:21:39,252
(Warming up his naked upper body)

469
00:21:41,762 --> 00:21:44,462
(Picking up)

470
00:21:45,162 --> 00:21:46,431
(He heads downstairs with food containers.)

471
00:21:46,432 --> 00:21:47,732
Why do you have food containers?

472
00:21:48,402 --> 00:21:50,632
- You had them in the bag? - Yes.

473
00:21:51,572 --> 00:21:53,241
But you didn't pack pajamas.

474
00:21:53,242 --> 00:21:54,942
(Food containers are more important than pajamas.)

475
00:21:55,442 --> 00:21:58,141
I can't survive winter in Japan. It's way too cold.

476
00:21:58,142 --> 00:21:59,712
(He comes down to the kitchen with the containers.)

477
00:22:01,142 --> 00:22:02,582
The boxed meal...

478
00:22:03,652 --> 00:22:05,051
- A boxed meal? - You'll pack a boxed meal?

479
00:22:05,052 --> 00:22:06,682
- He's going to pack a boxed meal. - Did you...

480
00:22:07,782 --> 00:22:08,982
(Opening up)

481
00:22:09,652 --> 00:22:11,792
(Let me see.)

482
00:22:12,722 --> 00:22:15,262
(He takes out all kinds of ingredients from the fridge.)

483
00:22:16,232 --> 00:22:17,631
Just don't make fried rice.

484
00:22:17,632 --> 00:22:18,891
It's fried rice.

485
00:22:18,892 --> 00:22:20,201
(That's correct!)

486
00:22:20,202 --> 00:22:21,532
(Oh, dear me!)

487
00:22:21,832 --> 00:22:24,132
I'm suddenly getting so worried.

488
00:22:24,602 --> 00:22:25,731
You've had it, right?

489
00:22:25,732 --> 00:22:28,842
Right. His kimchi fried rice was unforgettable.

490
00:22:29,642 --> 00:22:32,212
(Kian84 brought kimchi fried rice on the field day.)

491
00:22:32,672 --> 00:22:34,381
(The flavor of the fried rice hit him pretty hard.)

492
00:22:34,382 --> 00:22:36,512
I can still taste the oil in my mouth.

493
00:22:37,012 --> 00:22:38,212
You changed the recipe, right?

494
00:22:38,282 --> 00:22:39,721
- You changed it, right? - I did.

495
00:22:39,722 --> 00:22:41,522
I improved it about three steps from the old recipe.

496
00:22:41,622 --> 00:22:43,191
- What a relief. - Three steps?

497
00:22:43,192 --> 00:22:44,322
He should've improved it more.

498
00:22:46,522 --> 00:22:49,162
(He takes out various ingredients from the fridge.)

499
00:22:49,832 --> 00:22:51,792
(Placing them down)

500
00:22:52,962 --> 00:22:55,362
He's going to a boxed meal with other boxed meals.

501
00:22:57,072 --> 00:22:58,932
Well, Ito Junji...

502
00:22:59,172 --> 00:23:01,142
can probably afford to eat whatever he wants.

503
00:23:01,342 --> 00:23:03,012
So cooking was probably the best thing I could do.

504
00:23:03,212 --> 00:23:06,111
He can't buy my food at markets or restaurants.

505
00:23:06,112 --> 00:23:07,712
That's why I decided to cook.

506
00:23:07,942 --> 00:23:10,081
I bought some ingredients...

507
00:23:10,082 --> 00:23:12,252
to make kimchi fried rice which is my best dish.

508
00:23:13,322 --> 00:23:16,152
(He bought the ingredients the night before.)

509
00:23:16,392 --> 00:23:18,451
(Meat)

510
00:23:18,452 --> 00:23:20,721
(Kimchi)

511
00:23:20,722 --> 00:23:23,232
(Eggs)

512
00:23:24,162 --> 00:23:26,331
(Stir-Fry84 carefully picks up the ingredients.)

513
00:23:26,332 --> 00:23:27,832
Why do you keep looking for oil?

514
00:23:28,432 --> 00:23:29,632
No.

515
00:23:29,902 --> 00:23:32,302
My fried rice never fails.

516
00:23:32,732 --> 00:23:34,942
I've never failed with this dish. It always comes out tasty.

517
00:23:36,002 --> 00:23:37,611
I can't make it look nice.

518
00:23:37,612 --> 00:23:39,612
But when it comes to flavors, no other fried rice can beat mine.

519
00:23:39,682 --> 00:23:41,311
I am very good at...

520
00:23:41,312 --> 00:23:43,782
making the flavorful taste of fried rice.

521
00:23:44,452 --> 00:23:47,482
(He will serve his flavorful kimchi fried rice to his idol.)

522
