1390
00:59:26,809 --> 00:59:27,838
Right.

1391
00:59:27,839 --> 00:59:30,409
But I get that paid back to me in the end, right?

1392
00:59:30,909 --> 00:59:32,548
But I get that paid back to me in the end, right?

1393
00:59:32,549 --> 00:59:34,479
- What are you saying? - That's a loan.

1394
00:59:34,809 --> 00:59:36,718
Sorry? But you will be getting a loan.

1395
00:59:36,719 --> 00:59:39,288
But I will keep paying 550 dollars.

1396
00:59:39,289 --> 00:59:40,548
But you got a loan.

1397
00:59:40,549 --> 00:59:41,819
- A loan of 20,000 dollars? - Yes.

1398
00:59:42,159 --> 00:59:43,718
(You're right.)

1399
00:59:43,719 --> 00:59:44,818
You got a loan.

1400
00:59:44,819 --> 00:59:46,588
I studied a lot,

1401
00:59:46,589 --> 00:59:47,728
but I got things mixed up.

1402
00:59:47,729 --> 00:59:48,899
It's not a savings plan.

1403
00:59:49,659 --> 00:59:51,458
Why would you get money back after getting a loan?

1404
00:59:51,459 --> 00:59:52,569
Well...

1405
00:59:52,929 --> 00:59:55,799
I don't quite remember it right now. But...

1406
00:59:56,069 --> 00:59:57,569
- Bring me the beating stick. - Well...

1407
00:59:58,369 --> 01:00:00,939
Just stay in the same place. Don't think about moving.

1408
01:00:02,079 --> 01:00:03,608
It's my first time doing this.

1409
01:00:03,609 --> 01:00:04,709
It's understandable.

1410
01:00:05,549 --> 01:00:06,848
- Right. - It's understandable.

1411
01:00:06,849 --> 01:00:08,479
- It was new to me. - It's your first time.

1412
01:00:08,619 --> 01:00:10,248
So I can get a personal loan...

1413
01:00:10,249 --> 01:00:12,289
of 20,000 dollars from the company.

1414
01:00:13,589 --> 01:00:14,919
- Thank you. - No problem.

1415
01:00:15,119 --> 01:00:16,388
This is so hard.

1416
01:00:16,389 --> 01:00:18,828
(This is so hard.)

1417
01:00:18,829 --> 01:00:20,628
- Thank you. Bye. - Thank you. Bye.

1418
01:00:20,629 --> 01:00:23,729
(Kang Yong got his first-ever loan.)

1419
01:00:26,529 --> 01:00:27,529
(Letting out a sigh)

1420
01:00:28,669 --> 01:00:31,939
(Feeling heavy)

1421
01:00:32,539 --> 01:00:34,508
(Spacing out)

1422
01:00:34,509 --> 01:00:37,109
Numbers are so hard to deal with.

1423
01:00:37,679 --> 01:00:40,478
Everything is hard at first.

1424
01:00:40,479 --> 01:00:42,118
- You feel so drained. - Right.

1425
01:00:42,119 --> 01:00:43,119
It's not an area that gets covered...

1426
01:00:43,120 --> 01:00:44,148
- by studying. - Right.

1427
01:00:44,149 --> 01:00:45,178
- It's about experience. - It's about experience.

1428
01:00:45,179 --> 01:00:46,189
Right.

1429
01:00:46,949 --> 01:00:48,088
Gosh, I feel hungry.

1430
01:00:48,089 --> 01:00:51,259
(He keeps walking while feeling hungry.)

1431
01:00:52,059 --> 01:00:53,689
I should ask him first.

1432
01:00:56,899 --> 01:00:57,929
Kang Yong.

1433
01:00:58,769 --> 01:01:01,229
- Why are you so late? - I just got here.

1434
01:01:02,339 --> 01:01:03,469
- What's up? - Pardon?

1435
01:01:03,899 --> 01:01:05,408
It's my one-and-only variety show producer colleague...

1436
01:01:05,409 --> 01:01:06,909
with whom I joined the company in the same year.

1437
01:01:07,439 --> 01:01:08,539
- The same year. - I see.

1438
01:01:09,839 --> 01:01:11,209
- Hello? - Hey, Sang Min.

1439
01:01:11,779 --> 01:01:12,849
Hey, Kang Yong.

1440
01:01:13,049 --> 01:01:15,179
Can you spare some time later?

1441
01:01:15,349 --> 01:01:17,619
- The 13th floor. - Right.

1442
01:01:18,049 --> 01:01:20,519
Come up to the cafe when I call you.

1443
01:01:21,219 --> 01:01:23,088
He was the assistant director of "Where Is My Home."

1444
01:01:23,089 --> 01:01:24,289
We joined the company in the same year.

1445
01:01:24,889 --> 01:01:26,129
He must know a lot then.

1446
01:01:26,329 --> 01:01:30,259
He moved to a place very close to the office last year.

1447
01:01:30,999 --> 01:01:33,768
Since he recently found a place,

1448
01:01:33,769 --> 01:01:37,799
I thought I could get a few tips based on that.

1449
01:01:38,199 --> 01:01:40,409
That was why I decided to spend some time chatting with him.

1450
01:01:40,939 --> 01:01:42,279
- Since he has the experience. - Right.

1451
01:01:43,039 --> 01:01:45,909
- What's up? - I took my afternoon off today.

1452
01:01:46,879 --> 01:01:48,149
And I will look for a new house.

1453
01:01:48,579 --> 01:01:49,618
- You're planning to move? - Yes.

1454
01:01:49,619 --> 01:01:51,078
You live in Sangam.

1455
01:01:51,079 --> 01:01:52,449
- You live right here. - Right.

1456
01:01:52,819 --> 01:01:54,249
But as for me...

1457
01:01:54,719 --> 01:01:56,759
- You spend more time here anyway. - I... Right.

1458
01:01:57,389 --> 01:01:59,088
I live there just to reduce time...

1459
01:01:59,089 --> 01:02:00,859
- for my commute. - Right.

1460
01:02:01,359 --> 01:02:02,928
- Sangam isn't... - Variety show producers...

1461
01:02:02,929 --> 01:02:04,198
usually spend all night working.

1462
01:02:04,199 --> 01:02:05,498
It's better for producers to live near the office.

1463
01:02:05,499 --> 01:02:06,528
Right. He lives very close.

1464
01:02:06,529 --> 01:02:07,568
They have to spend time at the office anyway.

1465
01:02:07,569 --> 01:02:09,039
I don't spend much time at home.

1466
01:02:09,099 --> 01:02:11,269
- Where are you going? - Well,

1467
01:02:11,599 --> 01:02:15,168
I'm going to check out places in Gangseo-gu.

1468
01:02:15,169 --> 01:02:16,979
- Right. - There's a reason for this.

1469
01:02:18,209 --> 01:02:20,178
I didn't want to live too close to the office.

1470
01:02:20,179 --> 01:02:21,208
Right.

1471
01:02:21,209 --> 01:02:22,779
I want it to be close, but not too close.

1472
01:02:23,119 --> 01:02:24,878
If I wake up and see the office building,

1473
01:02:24,879 --> 01:02:26,618
- that would feel a bit... - I can see the office building.

1474
01:02:26,619 --> 01:02:27,989
- How does it feel? - It isn't easy.

1475
01:02:28,919 --> 01:02:30,459
It's not that pleasant.

1476
01:02:30,989 --> 01:02:33,089
Why is that? Isn't it better to be close to the office?

1477
01:02:33,189 --> 01:02:34,189
The seniors will call you out.

1478
01:02:34,190 --> 01:02:36,159
- You have to live away. - Really?

1479
01:02:36,299 --> 01:02:37,328
You have to be at an awkward distance...

1480
01:02:37,329 --> 01:02:38,528
- when you are called for. - Right!

1481
01:02:38,529 --> 01:02:39,998
- Not too close but not too far. - Then,

1482
01:02:39,999 --> 01:02:42,098
what is the most reasonable distance?

1483
01:02:42,099 --> 01:02:44,468
In terms of public transportation, it should be a 30-minute ride.

1484
01:02:44,469 --> 01:02:45,638
Around 30 minutes?

1485
01:02:45,639 --> 01:02:46,838
- Around that much. - Right.

1486
01:02:46,839 --> 01:02:48,438
Did you go when the seniors called for you?

1487
01:02:48,439 --> 01:02:49,608
- What? - Did you go?

1488
01:02:49,609 --> 01:02:50,679
- Me? - Yes.

1489
01:02:51,339 --> 01:02:52,879
I usually never got called out.

1490
01:02:54,079 --> 01:02:55,518
- There's this. - Really?

1491
01:02:55,519 --> 01:02:57,279
Seniors have preferences as well.

1492
01:02:57,879 --> 01:02:59,149
I wasn't called out as well.

1493
01:02:59,249 --> 01:03:00,418
I lived in Mok-dong, but I was never called out.

1494
01:03:00,419 --> 01:03:01,788
- I wasn't called out. - Never.

1495
01:03:01,789 --> 01:03:03,118
But Kang Yong is someone who would be called out.

1496
01:03:03,119 --> 01:03:04,388
- Surely. - Right.

1497
01:03:04,389 --> 01:03:06,328
- There are certain tasks. - Right.

1498
01:03:06,329 --> 01:03:07,759
(I will go as well when needed.)

1499
01:03:08,289 --> 01:03:10,099
Have you ever done a lump-sum deposit rental?

1500
01:03:10,299 --> 01:03:11,928
Yes. I got a lump-sum deposit rental.

1501
01:03:11,929 --> 01:03:13,199
Didn't you get scammed?

1502
01:03:14,469 --> 01:03:15,938
- Really? - Right.

1503
01:03:15,939 --> 01:03:17,038
- What? - The "Where Is My Home" producer...

1504
01:03:17,039 --> 01:03:18,098
went through a lump-sum deposit rental scam?

1505
01:03:18,099 --> 01:03:19,809
- My goodness. - No way.

1506
01:03:19,857 --> 01:03:21,787
- I got a lump-sum deposit rental. - Didn't you get scammed?

1507
01:03:22,399 --> 01:03:23,499
- Really? - Right.

1508
01:03:24,099 --> 01:03:25,138
- What? - The "Where Is My Home" producer...

1509
01:03:25,139 --> 01:03:26,139
went through a lump-sum deposit rental scam?

1510
01:03:26,140 --> 01:03:27,208
- My goodness. - No way.

1511
01:03:27,209 --> 01:03:30,139
- Oh, my. - It happened before the show.

1512
01:03:30,379 --> 01:03:32,549
He's a smart man...

1513
01:03:32,879 --> 01:03:35,049
- who has knowledge in the field. - You can still get scammed.

1514
01:03:35,149 --> 01:03:36,778
- That's right. - Being smart doesn't help.

1515
01:03:36,779 --> 01:03:38,588
- You can't get all the information. - It can't be helped.

1516
01:03:38,589 --> 01:03:40,648
- Being smart doesn't help. - I guess there are many scams.

1517
01:03:40,649 --> 01:03:41,719
So many.

1518
01:03:42,019 --> 01:03:43,459
How did you fall for the lump-sum deposit scam?

1519
01:03:43,619 --> 01:03:46,889
It might be that they weren't out to scam you.

1520
01:03:46,989 --> 01:03:49,228
If the property price falls...

1521
01:03:49,229 --> 01:03:50,858
and the landlord can't return your deposit,

1522
01:03:50,859 --> 01:03:52,128
you don't get your money back.

1523
01:03:52,129 --> 01:03:53,229
That's right.

1524
01:03:53,369 --> 01:03:54,839
That's why you need to get a surety bond.

1525
01:03:55,039 --> 01:03:56,598
If you get a surety bond,

1526
01:03:56,599 --> 01:04:00,509
- the insurance company pays you. - Yes.

1527
01:04:00,669 --> 01:04:02,209
Didn't you get a surety bond back then?

1528
01:04:02,609 --> 01:04:04,409
- It was a newly built apartment. - Okay.

1529
01:04:04,879 --> 01:04:07,209
You can't get it if there's no officially assessed land price.

1530
01:04:07,379 --> 01:04:08,818
Really?

1531
01:04:08,819 --> 01:04:10,419
- Then you can't get it. - Gosh, it's hard.

1532
01:04:10,619 --> 01:04:12,219
- It is, right? It's really hard. - Yes.

1533
01:04:13,019 --> 01:04:15,619
So I should get a surety bond for the lump-sum deposit rental.

1534
01:04:16,359 --> 01:04:18,829
Give up on the things you can live without.

1535
01:04:18,959 --> 01:04:20,888
That might be the size of the house or...

1536
01:04:20,889 --> 01:04:22,159
You're right. I should give up on a few things.

1537
01:04:22,429 --> 01:04:23,798
You need to look into it in detail.

1538
01:04:23,799 --> 01:04:25,499
When you draw up a contract,

1539
01:04:25,629 --> 01:04:27,499
- check the special conditions. - Special conditions.

1540
01:04:27,999 --> 01:04:30,099
Check the open-end mortgage.

1541
01:04:30,199 --> 01:04:32,669
Check the date you reported a change of address.

1542
01:04:32,939 --> 01:04:34,008
Don't trust the realtor too much.

1543
01:04:34,009 --> 01:04:35,739
That's right. That's the most important tip.

1544
01:04:37,209 --> 01:04:39,149
Why are there so many things to check? Seriously.

1545
01:04:39,509 --> 01:04:41,079
- I'm new to this, so... - Thank goodness you met him.

1546
01:04:42,119 --> 01:04:44,279
Okay. I need to get going now.

1547
01:04:44,649 --> 01:04:45,949
- I need to head down. - Okay.

1548
01:04:46,149 --> 01:04:47,448
- I'll get going. - I'll keep in touch.

1549
01:04:47,449 --> 01:04:48,559
- Okay. Keep in touch. - Okay.

1550
01:04:50,759 --> 01:04:52,028
I need to hurry up.

1551
01:04:52,029 --> 01:04:54,689
(Kang Yong moves hurriedly.)

1552
01:04:56,199 --> 01:04:57,329
All right.

1553
